      "nets": ["VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch), inside the block titled 'Decoupling Capacitors', the row of parallel VCC–GND parts reads C9 (4.7u), C1 (4.7u), C2 (100n), R11 (10k), C4 (100n), C5 (100n), C6 (100n). A 10 kΩ resistor (R11) is wired directly between the VCC and GND rails, and there is no C3 anywhere in the drawing.",
      "expected": "The specification's power section states the VCC–GND decoupling bank is all capacitors: 'C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 — 100 nF each, VCC–GND (local bypass)'. The position R11 occupies should hold a 100 nF bypass capacitor (C3); a resistor is the wrong component type for a decoupling position, and C3 is missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Decoupling Capacitors block, page 1 (root, PCB.kicad_sch): C9 4.7u | C1 4.7u | C2 100n | R11 10k | C4 100n | C5 100n | C6 100n — all drawn in parallel between the VCC arrow and the GND arrow"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2, C3, C4, C5, C6, C8 — 100 nF each, VCC–GND (local bypass)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The intended 100 nF high-frequency bypass (C3) is absent, weakening decoupling of the VCC rail, while the 10 kΩ R11 instead acts as a continuous DC load on the rail (and provides no decoupling). This can raise rail noise and reduce stability margin for the MCU/peripherals relative to the reference design.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build matches the spec on the NFC, display, touch, reset and SWD blocks, but the root-sheet 'Decoupling Capacitors' bank contains a 10 kΩ resistor (R11) where the spec's 100 nF bypass C3 should be (C3 is missing) — a wrong-component-type deviation that removes a decoupling cap and adds a resistive load on VCC."
}

